<% content_for :title, "Pick Ups & Deliveries - #{current_organization.name}" %>

<div class="px-4 py-6 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
  <%#
    The date *range* question belongs on the index, not here. A grid draws a month or a week; hand
    it "3 March to 19 August" and there is nothing for it to render. /distributions is the same data
    as a list and already has the range filter, so this points at it rather than growing a filter
    the calendar could not honour. See docs/design-decisions.md.
  %>
  <%= render "shared/essentials/page_header",
        title: "Pick ups & deliveries",
        subtitle: safe_join([
          "See when each distribution is due out, or subscribe to this calendar from your own. ",
          "To pick a date range instead, ",
          link_to("search all distributions", distributions_path,
                  class: "font-medium text-brand-700 underline hover:text-brand-800"),
          "."
        ]),
        actions: essentials_link_button("Copy calendar URL", "javascript:void(0)",
                   variant: :secondary, icon: "bi-clipboard",
                   id: "copy-calendar-button", data: {url: hashed_calendar_path}) %>

  <%#
    The toolbar is ours, not FullCalendar's. Its own is three buttons filled `rgb(44,62,80)` at a
    4px radius and 16px text, beside a 28px/400 title -- a page's worth of primary-looking chrome
    for moving the month, on a page whose real action is a quiet secondary. The grid is restyled in
    CSS the way select2 is; these are cheap to own outright, and owning them means a library
    upgrade cannot silently revert them. See design.md.

    "‹ Prev" and "Next ›" rather than bare chevrons: design.md reserves icon-only for a repeating
    row action, and this is the shape the pager already uses for the same job. The `aria-label`
    extends the visible word rather than replacing it, which is what 2.5.3 asks -- and it is set
    from the controller, because these step a month in one view and a week in the other two.
  %>
  <%= render "shared/essentials/card" do %>
    <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3"
         data-controller="calendar">
      <%# `aria-live`: the buttons change the grid without navigating, so without this nothing
          tells a screen reader which month is now on screen. %>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900"
          data-calendar-target="title" aria-live="polite"></h2>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
        <%#
          Month, Week and List, and no Day: over a year, 22 days had any distribution at all, mean
          1.9, and 13 of those held exactly one. `aria-pressed` rather than a radio group, because
          these toggle a state rather than submit a value.

          List is its own button because it is its own view. It used to be what "Week" rendered as
          below 992px, which made one label mean two things -- and since the list was also the
          default there, Week arrived pressed and its button did nothing.
        %>
        <div class="inline-flex overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-slate-300"
             role="group" aria-label="Calendar view">
          <% [["month", "Month"], ["week", "Week"], ["list", "List"]].each_with_index do |(value, label), index| %>
            <%= button_tag label, type: "button",
                  class: "px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-slate-700 transition-colors " \
                         "hover:bg-slate-50 aria-pressed:bg-slate-100 aria-pressed:text-slate-900 " \
                         "focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-brand-600 " \
                         "#{"border-l border-slate-300" if index.positive?}",
                  "aria-pressed": "false",
                  data: {calendar_view: value, action: "calendar#switchView",
                         calendar_target: "viewButton"} %>
          <% end %>
        </div>

        <%#
          Jumping to a month in another year. Prev and Next move one step, so before this March next
          year was seven clicks away and last December was five.

          Two selects rather than one `<input type="month">`, which is a picker in Chrome and Edge
          and a bare text box expecting "2026-08" in desktop Firefox and Safari. The year list is
          bounded by this organization's own data; the controller adds a year if Prev or Next walks
          past either end. Two labels rather than one, because they are two controls.
        %>
        <%= select_tag "calendar_month",
              options_for_select(Date::MONTHNAMES.compact.each_with_index.map { |name, index| [name, index] }),
              class: essentials_inline_select_classes(size: :sm),
              aria: {label: "Month"},
              data: {calendar_target: "monthSelect", action: "calendar#jumpTo"} %>
        <%= select_tag "calendar_year",
              options_for_select(@calendar_years.to_a),
              class: essentials_inline_select_classes(size: :sm),
              aria: {label: "Year"},
              data: {calendar_target: "yearSelect", action: "calendar#jumpTo"} %>

        <%#
          Today stays pressable even while today is on screen, where it does nothing. It was dimmed
          for a day and that is reverted deliberately: the case against disabled controls is about
          ones that *gate* a task, but every calendar a reader already uses -- Google, Outlook,
          Apple, Notion -- keeps Today live, and pressing it here costs nothing at all. A no-op is a
          smaller price than a control someone has to reason about. See docs/design-decisions.md.
        %>
        <%= button_tag "Today", type: "button",
              class: essentials_button_classes(variant: :secondary, size: :sm),
              data: {action: "calendar#today"} %>
        <%= button_tag type: "button", "aria-label": "Previous month",
              class: essentials_button_classes(variant: :secondary, size: :sm),
              data: {action: "calendar#previous", calendar_target: "stepButton",
                     calendar_step: "Previous"} do %>
          <i class="bi-chevron-left" aria-hidden="true"></i> Prev
        <% end %>
        <%= button_tag type: "button", "aria-label": "Next month",
              class: essentials_button_classes(variant: :secondary, size: :sm),
              data: {action: "calendar#next", calendar_target: "stepButton",
                     calendar_step: "Next"} do %>
          Next <i class="bi-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <%# FullCalendar renders into here; see calendar_controller.js. %>
      <div id="calendar" class="fc min-h-[36rem] w-full" data-calendar-target="grid"></div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
